    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pie and mash is London working-class food: a minced beef pie in shortcrust pastry, served with smooth mash and a vivid green parsley liquor sauce. The original liquor was made from the water used to cook jellied eels; the modern version is a sharp parsley sauce made with stock. The combination of buttery mash, rich pie, and the sharpness of the liquor is the point."
          }
        ]
